  "verbalization": "Levomilnacipran is implicated in the pathogenesis of Major Depressive Disorder (MDD) through a chain of indications that connect it to Anxiety Disorder, which in turn links to medications such as Nefazodone, Vortioxetine, and Desvenlafaxine. These medications are known to have antidepressant properties, suggesting a potential role for Levomilnacipran in the treatment of MDD. The shared indication of Anxiety Disorder across these pathways implies a possible overlap in mechanisms, such as the modulation of neurotransmitter systems or the influence of serotonin and norepinephrine. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, though indirect, relationship, possibly reflecting the use of Levomilnacipran in combination with other antidepressants. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in assessing the repurposing of Levomilnacipran for MDD.",
